Title: Array of nullable generic parameter has unexpected default value
Description: I have the following structure:
```
class MyClass<T> {
  public T? array;

  MyClass() {
    array = new T?[1];
  }
}

struct MyStruct {
  string fields;
}
```

Now let's say I do the following:
```
MyClass<MyStruct> instance = new();
Console.WriteLine(instance.array[0] is null);
```

I would expect to see `True` however what I get is `False`. The array initializes itself with a bunch of empty structs while I would expect a bunch of `null`.

